---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../../site.config';
import { aboutListings, adNotice, buyerAdvice, classifiedTerm } from '../../lib/copy';
const e = site.entity;
---
<Base title={`About ${site.name} and how listings are sourced`} description={`Who runs ${site.name}, how land ads and ${e.one} listings work, and what Basic and Verified mean.`} path="/about/" crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', url: '/' }, { name: 'About', url: '/about/' }]}>
  <h1>About {site.name}</h1>
  <p class="lead">{site.name} is an independent site for rural land for sale and the {e.many} who sell it, run by {site.owner}. It is not a brokerage, takes no commission, and is paid only for land ads and Verified {e.one} listings, as described below.</p>

  <h2 id="land">Land for sale</h2>
  <p>{adNotice} Each ad costs {classifiedTerm} and runs from the day it goes live; it is removed after its end date unless the seller renews it. Acreage, price and features are what the seller tells us. Ads are ordered newest first, and nobody can pay to appear higher.</p>
  <p>{buyerAdvice}</p>
  <p><a href="/sell-your-land/">Sell your land</a></p>

  <h2>Where {e.one} listings come from</h2>
  <p>Details come from each {e.one}’s own public website and profile pages, and from submissions sent with our form. We record the source and the date each listing was last checked or changed, and show that date on the page. We do not publish ratings or reviews: when a fact is unknown the listing says “Not listed”.</p>
  <p>To fix a mistake, use <a href="/add-your-business/">the add or update form</a>. {e.Many} who stop trading are removed.</p>
  <h2 id="listings">Basic and Verified {e.one} listings</h2>
  {aboutListings.map((p) => <p>{p}</p>)}
  <p>See <a href="/listing-plans/">listing plans</a> for prices and how the check works.</p>
</Base>
